348:
In lieu of the ten percent bail deposit, any person for whom bail has been set may execute the bail bond with or without sureties which bond may be secured by:
A. Cash. By a deposit with the chief of police of an amount equal to the required cash bail;
B. Property. By real estate located within Barrow or Gwinnett County with unencumbered equity, not exempted, owned by the accused or surety, valued at double the amount of bail set in the bond;
C. Professional. By a professional bail bondsman authorized by the chief of police and in compliance with the rules and regulations for execution of a surety bail bond.
(Ord. 241 § 2, 1998)

351:
A. Applications. In order to be considered for a certificate of authority, the prospective bondsman, whether individual, partnership or corporation must submit a letter of intent and an application to the chief of police. Applications shall be specific as it relates to the nature of the applicant and shall be individually submitted for each person who will have a power of attorney extended for writing bonds.
B. Corporations. The following documents will be provided with a corporation's application:
1. Certified copies of the articles of the corporation;
2. Current certificate of good standing from the Secretary of State;
3. A list of all duly elected members of the board of directors;
4. A list of all duly elected officers;
5. A list of all employees that pertain to Gwinnett County or the city;
6. A biographical sketch of each person or entity listed above;
7. A corporate resolution duly signed by the appropriate officers, affixed the corporate seal, stating that the corporation, by and through its duly authorized agents, is permitted to transact surety business in the state of Georgia and in the county of Barrow and Gwinnett and that such authority includes the power to execute and guarantee bail bond obligations or contracts to which the state or county is or may be a party;
8. A list of all bail bondsman with which the corporation or any individual listed above has been affiliated with during the past ten years as of the date of filing the application;
9. A list of all individuals or entities which will be authorized to sign or act on behalf of the bonding company and the accompanying powers of attorney;
10. The name and address of the individual who shall be authorized to accept service of process, such individual must be a resident of Barrow or Gwinnett County;
11. Such other relevant information as may be requested by the chief of police;
12. Current financial statement of the applicant to be submitted not more than thirty days from the date of application.
C. Other Applications. If the applicant is an entity other than a corporation, such as a partnership, joint venture or sole proprietor, then the following information shall be provided:
1. A list of all partners, including all parties that have an equitable interest in the partnership or operation of the sole proprietorship;
2. Any individual or entity who is entitled to receive any valuable consideration, financial or otherwise from the operation of the bail bond business;
3. A list of those individuals who will be signing on behalf of the applicant and the accompanying powers of attorney;
4. If a partnership or joint venture, a current certified copy of the partnership or joint venture agreement with all amendment, such information to be kept current from the date of application;
5. A biographical sketch of each person or entity listed above;
6. A list of all surety companies with which the entity or individuals listed in subsection (C)(l) through (4). have been affiliated with pertaining to Barrow or Gwinnett County, or the city, during the past ten years as of the date of filing this application;
7. The name and address of the individual who shall be authorized to accept service of process, such individual must be a resident of Gwinnett or Barrow County;
8. Such other relevant information as may be required by the chief of police;
9. Current financial statement of the applicant to be submitted not more than thirty days from the date of application.
D. Fingerprints and Photographs. Owners and agents of the professional bonding entity, subsequent to the submission of their biographical sketches, must agree to be finger printed and photographed by the identification section of the city police department and to pay such costs as is necessary to accomplish same.
(Ord. 241 § 5, 1998)

368:
